#: includes/Privacy.php:103
msgid "Suggested text:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Privacy.php:104
msgid "We use Navexa AgeCheck to verify the age of customers who order age-restricted products. When you start an age check at checkout, we send Navexa AgeCheck the shipping address of the order you are about to place and, when you have entered them and the order ships to your US billing address, your billing name and billing address, for the age check. When such an order is placed, we send its shipping address and an order reference, and, when no age check was done at checkout, your billing name, billing address and email address, and Navexa AgeCheck may email you a link to verify your age for that order. If you have an account with us, we also send a keyed reference to your account (the reference is not your name, email address or account number), so that a returning customer who passed an age check here recently may not have to verify again. When returning-customer checks are on and you check out as a guest, we also send Navexa AgeCheck your billing email address when you start an age check, so that if you passed a check here recently Navexa can email you a one-time code that lets you skip a new one; Navexa keeps the address encrypted with your check, and a one-way keyed code made from it that is tied to our store. You then verify on Navexa's own page (verify.navexa.co), where you enter your date of birth and, when asked, agree to a data check or photograph an ID document and take a selfie; we never see or keep your date of birth or ID images. Navexa uses Didit for the ID, selfie and liveness checks and, when the shipping address is your billing address, to check your billing name, billing address and date of birth against US data sources such as financial and credit-bureau records."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Privacy.php:105
msgid "We keep, with your order, the AgeCheck verification reference, whether your age check passed or failed and when, and a one-way hash of the shipping address that was checked. While you check out, your shopping session holds the verification reference. To stop abuse, we count age check attempts per session and per IP address for one hour, stored only as keyed hashes. Navexa's privacy policy explains how Navexa handles your data: https://navexa.co/privacy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Privacy.php:108
msgid "When you enter the store, we ask you to confirm that you are old enough. Your answer is remembered only in your own browser (local storage), so that we do not ask again for a while; it is not sent to us or to Navexa, and it is not an age verification."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Privacy.php:112
msgid "Before an age check starts, the checkout page runs a Cloudflare Turnstile security check, which loads a script from Cloudflare (challenges.cloudflare.com) and sends Cloudflare information about your browser; we send Cloudflare the check's result token and your IP address to confirm it. Cloudflare's Turnstile privacy addendum: https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/"
msgstr ""

